<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
        Test-only, and never merged into the app.

        A resident Analysis API session is a symbol table's worth of the Kotlin
        front end, and with android.jar on the classpath it does not fit the
        default 192 MB heap. The suite died with

            Failed to allocate a 672244 byte allocation ...
            growth limit 201326592; giving up on allocation

        and the damage read as something else entirely. The tests that ran out
        of memory were not the ones that allocated; they were the *next* ones,
        whose sessions then failed to open and answered every query with an
        empty list. Empty is a legitimate answer here, because LanguageService
        says nothing is an ordinary answer, so nothing threw and it looked
        instead as though extensions had stopped working.

        :app sets largeHeap and always has, so the shipped IDE was never
        affected. Only this harness was, by being quietly stricter than the
        environment the service actually runs in. The test manifest of
        :engine:fast carries the same fix for the same reason, found the same
        way.
    -->
    <application android:largeHeap="true" />

</manifest>
